  "source_brief": "# Access Ramp into Crater C-4\n\n**Site.** The rim of crater C-4, 6 m above the crater floor, 1.2 km from the landing pad. The wall is loose regolith over blocky material. The depot is on the rim; no recharging.\n\n**Structures.**\n\n1. Access ramp: 40 m long and 5 m wide, cut into the wall at a 15 percent grade (average cut depth 1.2 m, about 240 cubic metres) in four 10 m segments from the top down, with the cut from each segment hauled down as fill for the segment below.\n2. Rim turnaround: a level 10 m by 10 m apron at the top of the ramp, compacted so haulers can turn.\n3. Floor landing: a compacted 8 m by 8 m pad at the foot of the ramp.\n\n**Fleet.** EX1 and EX2 (excavators, 5000 Wh each), HL1 (hauler, 3000 Wh), CP1 (compactor, 3500 Wh) and SV1 (surveyor, 1500 Wh). Batteries are the whole budget.\n\n**Deadline.** 8 days.\n\n**Operational constraints.**\n\n- Segments are cut strictly from the top down; a segment is compacted before the next one is opened.\n- The surveyor checks the grade of every segment before compaction.\n- Only one robot may work inside a zone at a time.\n"
 },
